feat(admin-blocklist): rate-limit blocklist writes (60/min/IP)

Roadmap item 16 (partial — admin-blocklist was the only admin*.ts
route missing rateLimitCheck). 60 writes/min per IP shared across
add/remove for blacklist + whitelist combined.

Rationale: a hostile admin cookie (CSRF or session theft) shouldn't
be able to flood the blocklist table — each entry costs a row + an
audit_log mirror entry, so a tight burst could pollute both stores
with thousands of bogus rows.

Implementation:
- New gateRateLimit() helper folded into addEntry + deleteEntry.
- Bucket key = `admin-blocklist-write:${ip}` (shared across add+del).
- 429 with code RATE_LIMITED matches the shape of every other
  admin route's rate-limit response.

Build: 510 modules. 80/80 lib tests pass.